#### 7. Trivial `IsNotNull` Assertions (lines 28, 51, 59, 81)

`GetProduct`, `Search`, `GetAll`, and `ExportToCsv` assert only `IsNotNull`. These pass even if the data is completely wrong — an empty list, a corrupted CSV, or a mismatched product all pass `IsNotNull`.

**Fix (`SearchProducts`):**
```csharp
var results = _catalog.Search("Widget");
Assert.AreEqual(1, results.Count);
Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001", results[0].Sku);
